<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108021" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπευν-άομαι</span></b> , 
			Pass.
		, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐνάω</span>) only in fem. part.
		aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπευνηθεῖσα,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in wedlock with,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φοίβῳ ὑ.</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπευνασθεῖσα</span>
			) Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				3.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be under-bedded with</i> a thing, i. e. <i>lying</i> or
				<i>sitting upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρταλὶς . . ὑπευνηθεῖσα νεοσσοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					294
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπευνασθεῖσα</span> cod.
		opt.).</div>
